WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.268
-Are you aware of the comparison

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:04.337
that people are making between
you and Noah Centineo?

00:00:04.337 --> 00:00:07.273
[ Laughter ]

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:09.075
Have you heard -- You ever
heard -- You know Noah?

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.177
This is Noah Centineo
right here.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.578
People say you guys look alike.

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.047
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:16.616
-I wish I was that good-looking.

00:00:16.616 --> 00:00:18.852
-No. You are that good-looking.
-No.

00:00:18.852 --> 00:00:20.487
-Yeah, you are.
-No.

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:23.056
-And they're saying -- They're
saying that you actually --

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:26.893
-He might be able
to play my dad one day.

00:00:26.893 --> 00:00:28.961
-He'll play your dad?
-Yeah. Perfect.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:31.030
We have a clip.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:33.299
People say that you guys
even sound alike.

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:34.733
-Come on.
-Have you not heard this?

00:00:34.733 --> 00:00:36.869
-I've heard --
People have said that, but I --

00:00:36.869 --> 00:00:38.971
-Just listen. Here. Check this.
This is Noah Centineo.

00:00:38.971 --> 00:00:40.407
-I'm Noah Centineo.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:42.708
You might know me from "To All
the Boys I've Loved Before"

00:00:42.708 --> 00:00:44.376
or "Sierra Burgess" on Netflix.

00:00:44.376 --> 00:00:46.212
"Anyone else thinking
that Noah Centineo

00:00:46.212 --> 00:00:48.414
could have been a young
Mark Ruffalo? Just me?"

00:00:48.414 --> 00:00:49.548
It's not just you.

00:00:49.548 --> 00:00:51.884
Casting directors always
comparing me to him.

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:56.956
I even think I am Mark Ruffalo,
and space and time

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.158
is just a weird thing
that we can't understand.

00:00:59.158 --> 00:01:01.327
-Wow! Is that possible?
-Wow.

00:01:01.327 --> 00:01:04.363
-Could that be possible?

00:01:04.363 --> 00:01:07.634
-I -- Yeah. Wow. It's amazing.

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:10.269
He's way better-looking
than I was.

00:01:10.269 --> 00:01:11.771
-Really?
-Yeah. Are you kidding me?

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:13.873
-You were good-looking
when you were this --

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:17.109
-No. How old is he?
-He's probably like 15 or so.

00:01:17.109 --> 00:01:18.878
-No.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.746
I wish I looked like that.
I swear to God.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:22.481
-Well, actually,
we went on Instagram.

00:01:22.481 --> 00:01:25.118
We found a picture of you.
This is you when you were 15.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:27.887
I think it's not bad.
I think --

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:29.322
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:29.322 --> 00:01:31.724
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:34.626
-Wow!
-All right, now.

00:01:34.626 --> 00:01:36.396
-Similar. I mean, similar.
Come on.

00:01:36.396 --> 00:01:40.867
-Noah -- Noah, you're doing
way better than me, pal.

00:01:40.867 --> 00:01:43.135
-[ Laughs ]
-I wished I was you.

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:46.071
-You had it rough as a kid
with these braces, huh?

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:47.773
-Yeah.
-Holy moly.

00:01:47.773 --> 00:01:50.210
-Look at that. There's no teeth.
It's just all braces.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.245
-Wow! Those are real.
That's unbelievable.

00:01:52.245 --> 00:01:53.679
-That's what it used to be like.

00:01:53.679 --> 00:01:56.782
I'd go swimming and sink
to the bottom of the pool.

00:01:56.782 --> 00:01:59.852
-[ Laughs ]
I mean, that's major league.

00:01:59.852 --> 00:02:01.421
How long did you have them on?

00:02:01.421 --> 00:02:03.022
-That's some hardware.
Oh, too long.

00:02:03.022 --> 00:02:04.390
-Really?
-Well, I was supposed to

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.693
have them on for five years,
and I --

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:11.297
-Wow.
-I took them off a little early.

00:02:11.297 --> 00:02:14.200
-You took them off yourself?
-Yeah.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.468
-How?

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:18.004
-With pliers.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.472
-Did you really?

00:02:19.472 --> 00:02:22.342
-It was my major act
of rebellion in my youth.

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.943
-[ Laughs ]
Oh, my God. Your mom --

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.711
-My mom was like,
"What are you doing?!

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.480
-"That's more expensive
than the house!

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.181
-That's it! I've had it!
I've had it!

00:02:29.181 --> 00:02:30.616
-I've had it with you, Mark!"

00:02:30.616 --> 00:02:32.718
-You're going to have
crooked teeth your whole life!"

00:02:32.718 --> 00:02:35.354
And I was like, "I don't care!"

00:02:35.354 --> 00:02:39.058
-"I'm going to be in 'Avengers,'
Mom, one day! You'll see!"

00:02:39.058 --> 00:02:40.893
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:40.893 --> 00:02:42.161
"I'm the Hulk!"

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:45.765
-I'm sorry, Mom.
She's watching right now.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:48.134
-Yeah, it's great.
They turned out pretty great.

00:02:48.134 --> 00:02:50.469
Can we talk about
"Avengers: Endgame"?

00:02:50.469 --> 00:02:52.505
Because everyone's
excited about it, clearly.

00:02:52.505 --> 00:02:54.807
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:54.807 --> 00:03:00.046
I know. You got in trouble.
It comes out April 26th.

00:03:00.046 --> 00:03:02.648
So this is -- But this is --

00:03:02.648 --> 00:03:04.316
The last time you were on,
we talked about it,

00:03:04.316 --> 00:03:05.384
and we weren't really --

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.953
-Yeah, I got in
a lot of trouble.

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.421
-You really did.
-Yeah, I did.

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:11.657
And you thought it was funny.
"Ha-ha-ha."

00:03:11.657 --> 00:03:16.162
Next thing I know, Joe Russo
has fired me on Twitter.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:19.031
The President has created a fad.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:22.301
Now everyone's being fired
on Twitter.

00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:24.670
-Dude, that was --
-That's the one positive thing

00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:26.839
that will come out of this
presiden-- I'm sorry.

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.609
I'm not supposed to say
stuff like that.

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.977
-But Tom Holland,
who plays Spider-Man,

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:33.446
he's was known for --

00:03:33.446 --> 00:03:36.115
He spoiled a couple things,
and Marvel got real mad at him.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.483
-I love that guy.

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.785
-Are you guys allowed
to do press together, or no?

00:03:39.785 --> 00:03:42.254
-I just keep -- I'm going to
put him in front of me.

00:03:42.254 --> 00:03:43.822
-Yeah, exactly.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:46.059
-Just like a human
spoiler shield.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.661
-[ Laughs ]
That's hilarious.

00:03:48.661 --> 00:03:51.363
-I asked to be paired with him
during the press,

00:03:51.363 --> 00:03:55.367
and -- and -- they -- they --
they rejected that.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:58.137
-Oh, absolutely. They didn't
even let you guys even --

00:03:58.137 --> 00:04:00.173
-No, I was like,
"What about me and Tom H--"

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.807
I didn't even get "Holland" out.

00:04:01.807 --> 00:04:03.342
I was like,
"What about me and Tom H--"

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:06.312
"No! Absolutely not!"

00:04:06.312 --> 00:04:09.115
-Yeah, so now who are you on --
have to do the press with?

00:04:09.115 --> 00:04:11.617
-Chris Evans.
-Oh, hey.

00:04:11.617 --> 00:04:13.386
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:14.754
-I know.
-How cool is Chris Evans?

00:04:14.754 --> 00:04:18.157
-I can just sit there
and be beautiful.

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.359
[ Laughter ]

00:04:20.359 --> 00:04:22.862
-He's a good -- He's a stud.
-He's amazing. Aw, come on.

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.530
-It's Chris Evans. Come on.
-Chris Evans.

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:27.833
-He's perfect. We like him.

00:04:27.833 --> 00:04:29.601
-He's amazing at everything.
-Yeah.

00:04:29.601 --> 00:04:31.537
And he won't spoil anything.
-No, no, no.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.306
He's tight-lipped.
-Yeah, he's good.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.241
-He's Captain America.
-Yeah, of course.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:37.744
You're not allowed to do that.
-I'm just Bruce Banner.

00:04:37.744 --> 00:04:41.247
-That's -- Yeah, but I mean --
I want to ask you more questions

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.048
about the "Avengers"
if you don't mind,

00:04:43.048 --> 00:04:45.585
but when we come back. Okay.
More with Mark Ruffalo.

